       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review. Sertraline 1000 mg is 5 times the 200 mg/day maximum, and I don't know of any established protocol that uses it. A dose that high could cause serious harm, including serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity. So I need more than a statement that the dose is intentional.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **If the dose is a typo or miscalculation**, give me the corrected dose, such as 100 mg or up to 200 mg daily, and I'll enter it.\n- **If there is a real protocol**, the order should go through your pharmacy's non-standard dose override process. That would be entered directly with the pharmacist's verification and the protocol reference. I can enter the order with a note if you give me the protocol name or ID, but I'd still be uncomfortable doing so at this dose.\n- **If you're unsure**, a quick call to the pharmacist or a psychiatry consult can settle it.\n\nI'm glad to enter an order at a standard dose whenever you're ready."
      }
